      "The condition is $a > b > c$.",
      "The target inequality is $\frac{1}{a-b} + \frac{1}{b-c} \geq \frac{k}{a-c}$ for all such $a,b,c$."
    ],
    "error_step": "- $ a - b = b - c $",
    "error_reason": "This equality is not given and is not generally true for all $a>b>c$; it incorrectly assumes $b$ is the midpoint of $a$ and $c$.",
    "new_direction": "Let $x=a-b>0$ and $y=b-c>0$, so $a-c=x+y$, and minimize $(x+y)(1/x+1/y)$ to find the largest valid integer $k$."
